@startuml
' Which way one voice command goes: every decision between "Hey Jarvis"
' and what you hear. Render: projects/voice-assistant/render_architecture.sh
title One voice command - every decision

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3E0

start
:Satellite streams mic audio to HA (always);
if (openwakeword hears "Hey Jarvis"\nor "Dumbledore"? (wake-proxy)) then (no)
  stop
endif
if (the other satellite already took this wake word?) then (yes)
  #EEEEEE:This run dropped
  (error duplicate_wake_up_detected);
  stop
endif
:Record until silence (VAD);
:speech-to-phrase: audio -> nearest trained phrase;
if (close enough to a trained phrase?) then (no)
  #E1BEE7:stt-fallback: IndicConformer (Marathi)
  same audio -> Devanagari;
  if (clearly one of our songs?\n(local title match, then Spotify top 3)) then (yes)
    #E1BEE7:text = "play <title>";
  else (no)
    #FFCDD2:"No text recognized"
    run ends, nothing happens;
    stop
  endif
endif
if (matches "play {song}"?) then (yes)
  #E3F2FD:voice_play_song (4a);
  if (title in the song list?) then (yes)
    if (satellite's area is bedroom?) then (yes)
      #E3F2FD:Spotcast: play the track on the Pi;
    else (no)
      #E3F2FD:Spotcast: play the track on xero
      (reconnect the Bluetooth speaker first);
    endif
    :reply "Playing <title> - <artist>";
  else (no)
    :reply "<title> is not in your liked songs";
  endif
elseif (matches a sentence in voice_commands.yaml?) then (yes)
  #E8F5E9:that automation (4b): AC, fan speed,
  turn off everything, Spotify pause / next / volume;
  :its reply ("AC on", "Bedroom fan low", ...);
elseif (matches a built-in sentence?) then (yes)
  #FFF8E1:HA built-in intent (4c):
  turn on/off <name>, timers, time;
  :built-in reply ("Turned off the switch");
else (no)
  :reply "Sorry, I couldn't understand that"
  (rare: speech-to-phrase only returns
  phrases HA already knows);
endif
:Piper turns the reply into speech;
#EEEEEE:Reply URL sent to the satellite:
dropped (no speaker; plan-room-replies.md);
stop
@enduml
